id: pm-8patuh
title: "schema add-field accepts flag spellings the option parser splits or already owns implicitly, which can stop a command from starting"
description: "Reported by an independent review of the option-collision change and not yet reproduced here. A custom field flag or alias containing a pipe is stored as one spelling, but the option parser splits a flag declaration at a pipe, so a flag such as full|detail registered for list tries to register a second full option and the command fails during registration, before its action runs and whatever flags the user typed. Separately, an alias equal to the short help flag is accepted because help is supplied implicitly and the existing-option test does not see it, after which the short help flag demands a value. Both are flag-spelling validation gaps that predate the collision check."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[3]: "area:cli",schema,validation
created_at: "2026-11-22T21:23:51.347Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-22T21:23:51.347Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "Reproduce both cases in a scratch tracker and record the observed failure; schema add-field, profile apply and rename-field refuse a flag or alias that is not exactly one option spelling, with a typed refusal naming the spelling; The implicit help flags are reserved for every command a field is registered for; validate reports stored definitions with such spellings"
parent: pm-8jdc
risk: medium
confidence: medium
expected_result: A field flag that the parser would split or that shadows implicit help is refused at registration and reported by validate when already stored
